;; source-span-present — a claim must have at least one source-span
;; (REQ-KG-003 / REQ-KG-012).
;;
;; Booklogic port of the tbf:hasSourceSpan minCount constraint in
;; assets/shapes.ttl:
;;   sh:path tbf:hasSourceSpan ; sh:minCount 1 .
;;
;; minCount >= 1 lowers to a NEGATION over the source-span back-reference: a
;; claim is a violation when NO source-span row carries its id in
;; :source-span/claim-id (the projector populates that column as the back-ref to
;; the owning claim). ?focus is bound by the positive :where and threaded into
;; the negation, so this is a safe inline Cozo negation (no free var). The
;; constraint fires for a claim of ANY status that lacks provenance — unlike the
;; verified-derives sh:sparql shape, which restricts to verified claims.
;;
;; MESSAGE NOTE: pyshacl auto-generates the minCount message ("Less than 1
;; values on <...>->tbf:hasSourceSpan", as in the C0.2 golden); EXACT
;; pyshacl-message parity is a P2.3 concern. The human message below is clear
;; and stable for P2.2.
(defconstraint :source-span-present
  :message "Claim must have at least one source-span (minCount 1 on hasSourceSpan)."
  :path "https://example.org/book-knowledge#hasSourceSpan"
  :component "http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#MinCountConstraintComponent"
  :where [[?c :claim/id ?focus]]
  :not   [[?s :source-span/claim-id ?focus]])
